commit 5289c661877462f3caf6c4e136ad3c163f6fe15b
Author: Marat K <phpcraftdream@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 18:48:11 2026 +0200

    perf(runtime): OWN_CACHE_SIZE 4->16 + Tier-1 hit/miss counter (F2, task #501)
    
    Built the missing path-activation oracle for SegmentTable::contains_base's
    Tier-1 direct-mapped own_cache (CONTAINS_BASE_TIER1_HITS/_MISSES,
    bench-internals-gated, src/alloc_core/alloc_core.rs +
    src/alloc_core/segment_table.rs), then a Large-heavy workload
    (examples/r32_10_own_cache_tier1_thrash_gate.rs) to drive it -- exactly the
    instrument docs/perf/OPEN_ITEMS.md item 1's own text left open ("Tier-2-
    hash-probe-heavy workloads might show contains_base > 8.8%, open, not a
    proven floor") and R23-3 said could not be built "portably" (a benchmark
    cannot predict which OS-assigned addresses collide; this counter observes
    the resulting hit rate after the fact instead).
    
    Two false-start workload designs, both self-caught by the harness's own
    path-activation oracles before any wrong number was published:
    1. Free+realloc rotation at fixed K=64: measured exactly 50.00% hit rate,
       bit-identical at OWN_CACHE_SIZE=4 and =16 -- a redundant SECOND
       contains_base call inside AllocCore::dealloc's Large fallthrough
       (pre-existing, F6-shaped, out of this task's scope) always turns into a
       guaranteed hit, masking any real signal.
    2. K-sweep with the same free+realloc shape: still exactly 50.00% at EVERY
       K including K=4 -- every Large free unconditionally calls unregister,
       which evicts the base's OWN cache slot at the end of the very call that
       warmed it, so a repeatedly-freed base's cache entry can never survive to
       its next visit regardless of cache size.
    
    Correct shape: repeated in-place realloc (same size, no free, no
    unregister) rotating across K concurrently-LIVE Large objects, K swept over
    {4,8,16,24,32,48,64}, through HeapCore::realloc (the real
    #[global_allocator] entry point). Measured: 0.00% Tier-1 hit rate at
    OWN_CACHE_SIZE=4 for EVERY tested K including K=4 (even the smallest
    rotation fully thrashed the old cache); 99.99% at OWN_CACHE_SIZE=16 for
    K in {4,8}; K>=16 still thrashes at cache=16 (direct-mapped, not
    associative -- K==cache-size does not guarantee distinct buckets).
    
    Shipped OWN_CACHE_SIZE 4->16 plus a new compile-time power-of-two pin
    (cache_index's masking arithmetic requires it; none existed before).
    
    Latency (ns/op) delta is an HONEST NULL -- both before/after arms sit in
    the same ~24-29 ns/op noise band despite the dramatic hit-rate delta,
    consistent with item 1's own ~4 Ir component pricing (Tier-1 hit ~8.2 Ir
    vs Tier-2 miss ~12.0 Ir) being small against realloc's whole cost. No
    latency win is claimed.
    
    perf(runtime): alloc-xthread (which makes contains_base the always-on
    ownership check on every own-thread free/in-place-realloc) is in
    production's default feature set.
    
    Standing +/-10 raw-Ir churn kill gate NOT run (no Linux/Valgrind on this
    dev host, same constraint task #500 documented) -- argued, not measured,
    to stay flat (the change is a per-heap struct-size constant plus
    bench-internals-gated counter increments only, compiled out of a plain
    production build).
    
    Updated docs/perf/OPEN_ITEMS.md: closed F2, answered item 1's own open
    clause in place (struck through with an ANSWERED note), and corrected
    item 34's text (which had wrongly predicted this task would reuse task
    #500's macro_multiseg_steady_state harness -- that harness's churn step
    frees only ONE Large object per round, structurally unable to exercise
    OWN_CACHE_SIZE thrashing; a separate purpose-built K-sweep harness was
    needed instead).
    
    Fixed a pre-existing doc-hygiene test (architecture_test_file_count_
    matches_reality) that needed docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's tests/*.rs count
    updated 232->233 for this task's one new test file.
    
    See docs/perf/R32_10_OWN_CACHE_TIER1_THRASH_GATE.md for the full sweep,
    both false-start designs, raw logs, and the checked summary-CSV script
    (scripts/r32_10_own_cache_tier1_summary.mjs, headline claims asserted
    in-script per CLAUDE.md's derived-not-hand-typed rule).
    
